{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789809210,"nonce":"agfexwPcPYiYGMHumZ87sj1HV1M=","title":"tiered_on_invoke clones the shared-context Arc on every invocation","message":"beadie's TieredAdapter::on_invoke takes a compile closure that is 'static + Clone, so the interpreter clones Arc\u003cTieredSharedCtx\u003e into a fresh closure per call, compiled or not, before the fast path that compares the cached entry. That is two atomic RMWs per interpreted call on top of the tick. tiered_on_invoke was 2.6-3.8% of deltablue's main-thread samples (85cd9fc).\n\nOptions: a per-findex closure cached in the runtime (needs an Fn type the adapter accepts without a fresh Arc, e.g. a pointer-and-generation handle into a leaked context), or a beadie API that takes the closure by reference and only clones on submit. The steady-state path -- bead compiled, entry cached -- should be a tick and a compare.","files":null}]}